# Copy to /opt/mower/.env on the robot (deploy/install.sh does this once).
# Registry + repository the robot pulls from. CI publishes every tag to both
# docker.io/fxrbindi/mower_path_planning (default: ~9 MB/s from the home
# ISP) and ghcr.io/edwards414/mower_path_planning (~70 kB/s from the same
# line, Fastly path; keep as fallback). Root must be logged in to the
# registry (sudo docker login docker.io) while the repository is private.
IMAGE_REPO=docker.io/fxrbindi/mower_path_planning
# Release channel or exact version of IMAGE_REPO:
#   stable  = last v* tag (default)      main = every push to main      v0.6.0 = pinned
IMAGE_TAG=stable
# Host directory mounted as /home/mower/.mower in the container. Must be owned by
# uid 1000 (zones, sites, bags, firmware_sync.json, host.request live here).
MOWER_STATE_DIR=/home/cat/.mower
# rosbridge listen address: WireGuard/relay IP, or the LAN IP for a bench robot.
ROSBRIDGE_ADDRESS=10.77.0.2
# 0 = keep whatever firmware is on the STM32 (e.g. a CubeIDE debug build)
MOWER_FIRMWARE_SYNC=1
# u-blox ZED-F9P driver (mower_rs mower_gps) in the main container
# (/dev/gps_rtk -> /fix, /gps/status). false = no /fix at all; navigation then
# stays blocked by its health gate. Settings: src/mower_bringup/config/gps.yaml.
GPS=true
# Shown as robot_id in /robot/info (default: hostname)
MOWER_ROBOT_ID=
# 1 = mower-update.timer checks IMAGE_TAG every hour and updates when the robot is idle
MOWER_AUTO_UPDATE=1
# CPU frequency cap (kHz) while mower-update.sh downloads and unpacks an image.
# The LubanCat hard-reset during four pulls on 2026-10-07/08 with no kernel
# error and the journal cut mid-line; a 5 V / USB rail brownout under the
# pull's CPU + eMMC load is the working hypothesis. 1008000 = 1.0 GHz, 0 = no
# cap. Lifted before the stack restarts.
MOWER_UPDATE_MAX_FREQ_KHZ=1008000
# Fleet backend (docs/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md). Empty = no registration, no
# heartbeat, no remote relay (LAN only). The provision token is the fleet's
# install secret (wrangler secret put PROVISION_TOKEN on the backend).
MOWER_BACKEND_URL=https://api.mower.fxrbindi.com
MOWER_PROVISION_TOKEN=
MOWER_MODEL=lubancat
# Relay WebSocket URL put into the pairing QR (empty = LAN only). With the
# backend this is the app relay entry of this robot.
PAIR_RELAY_URL=wss://api.mower.fxrbindi.com/v1/relay/app
# 4G fallback uplink (host/mower-lte.sh, Quectel EC25 over QMI). The default
# route on wwan0 gets this metric; NetworkManager uplinks sit at 100, so LTE
# only carries traffic when Ethernet / Wi-Fi are gone.
MOWER_LTE_APN=internet
MOWER_LTE_METRIC=200
# Front camera publisher (host/mower-camera.sh): USB MJPG -> Rockchip MPP H.264
# -> mediamtx. Defaults shown; CAMERA_RTSP_URL empty = the local mediamtx.
CAMERA_DEVICE=/dev/video0
CAMERA_SIZE=1280x720
CAMERA_FPS=25
CAMERA_BPS=2000000
CAMERA_GOP=10
CAMERA_RTSP_URL=
# Interface(s) whose IPs MediaMTX offers as WebRTC ICE candidates (comma-separated;
# not docker0/tailscale0, which only slow the phone's ICE checks down).
WEBRTC_INTERFACES=eth1

# mower_rs (Rust) processes instead of their rclpy versions (src/mower_rs/README.md).
# RUST_STATUS: robot_status instead of heartbeat_node + robot_info_node +
#   telemetry_node (same topics and services; flip after the shadow comparison).
# RUST_ADAPTER: mower_adapter instead of flutter_adapter_node (same /adapter/*).
# RUST_GUARDS: velocity_command_guard for both guard instances; flip only after
#   a supervised drive with the app joystick and a navigation run.
# RUST_MUX: mower_rsd's mux module (mower_mux) instead of the C++ twist_mux,
#   only with RUST_DAEMON=true. It decides what reaches the final guard
#   (joystick over navigation, the navigation lock, the safety stop): the first
#   switch is a supervised drive, someone at the robot. RUST_MUX=false (or
#   RUST_DAEMON=false) brings the C++ twist_mux back, no new image needed.
# RUST_IMU: mower_imu instead of the wit_ros2_imu serial driver (same /imu/data).
# RUST_BRIDGE: mower_ws_bridge (pairing gate + rosbridge protocol + rosapi/topics)
#   instead of rosbridge_auth_proxy + rosbridge_websocket + rosapi.
# WS_BRIDGE_BUS: mower_ws_bridge on mower_bus instead of on an r2r node of its
#   own (same door, frames and error texts; the names only DDS has go through
#   the bus bridge). Needs RUST_BRIDGE. It is the app's only door, the in-app
#   update included, so switch it only while LAN SSH works: false = the
#   roll-back, no new image needed.
# RUST_RECORD: mower_record instead of path_record_node (same services and files).
#   It is the zone path recorder, not the bag recorder (RUST_RECORDER, below).
# RUST_NAV: mower_nav instead of nav_action_server (same actions, services and
#   safety heartbeat); flip only after a supervised navigation run.
# RUST_BATTERY: mower_battery instead of battery_state_node (same estimator and
#   BatteryState output).
# RUST_PID_AUTOTUNE: mower_pid_autotune instead of pid_autotune_node (same
#   /pid_autotune service, status JSON and base side channels).
# RUST_MAP: mower_map instead of map_manage_node (same services, latched maps,
#   /map_manage parameters; pixel-exact OpenCV ports).
# RUST_AGENT: mower_agent (Rust) instead of the Python fleet agent (same
#   registration, relay protocol, sessions, WHEP relay and TURN refresh).
# RUST_BASE: mower_base instead of ros2_control_node + mower_hardware +
#   diff_controller + joint_state_broadcaster (same /odom, /joint_states,
#   /mower_base/* and serial protocol; robot_state_publisher stays), and
#   instead of the odom_throttle process (mower_base publishes /odom_slow).
#   It is the drivetrain. Default on since 2026-10-08; false = the C++
#   chain (the roll-back, no new image needed). A robot still on the C++
#   chain is switched with someone present: docs/ROS_FREE_HANDOFF.md, 上機.
# RUST_LOCALIZE: mower_localize instead of the two robot_localization ekf_node
#   processes and navsat_transform_node (same node names, /odometry/local,
#   /odometry/global, /odometry/gps, /gps/filtered, odom->base_footprint and
#   map->odom, /toLL, /fromLL, /datum), and instead of the
#   global_odom_throttle process (it publishes /odometry/global_slow).
#   Default on since 2026-10-08; false = the C++ nodes. nav2 steers on its
#   map->odom, so the first switch of a robot is a supervised drive.
# RUST_DAEMON: run every module enabled above inside one mower_rsd process
#   (one r2r Context = one DDS participant) instead of one binary each. Node
#   names, topics, services and parameters are unchanged; the module set is
#   derived from the switches above plus GPS, and always includes the coverage
#   planner (mower_coverage, which has no switch: there is no rclpy version).
#   Default on; roll-back is RUST_DAEMON=false (one binary each).
# RUST_NAV_CORE: mower_nav steers with mower_nav_core, the in-process Rust port
#   of the nav2 servers (docs/ROS_FREE_PLAN.md Phase D), and nav2 is not
#   started (twist_mux, the guards and the rest stay). Needs RUST_DAEMON,
#   RUST_NAV and RUST_LOCALIZE true; the launch refuses to start otherwise. It
#   changes the code that drives the wheels, so the first switch of a robot is
#   a supervised outdoor run. false = nav2 (the roll-back, no new image needed).
RUST_STATUS=false
RUST_ADAPTER=false
RUST_RECORD=false
RUST_NAV=false
RUST_BATTERY=false
RUST_PID_AUTOTUNE=false
RUST_MAP=false
RUST_AGENT=false
RUST_GUARDS=false
RUST_MUX=false
RUST_IMU=false
RUST_BRIDGE=false
WS_BRIDGE_BUS=false
RUST_BASE=true
RUST_LOCALIZE=true
# RUST_STATIC_TF: mower_rsd's static_tf module (mower_static_tf) instead of
#   robot_state_publisher, only with RUST_DAEMON=true: the same URDF's fixed
#   joints on /tf_static (base_link, imu_link, gps_link, the cameras), the wheels
#   on /tf, /robot_description. RUST_STATIC_TF=false brings rsp back.
RUST_STATIC_TF=false
# RUST_RECORDER: mower_rsd's bag module (mower_recorder: recorder_manager,
#   bag_store, graph_snapshot) instead of the Python recorder of compose's
#   recorder service, which then sleeps (one owner of /mower_recorder/*); with
#   RUST_DAEMON=false the mower_recorder binary. mower-data-collection.sh
#   refuses to start while it is true (data collection in the module is E5-5).
#   It records the default profile from DDS (E5-3b); it stays false until the
#   owner's robot checks (an R2 upload, a supervised recording) and E5-7 make
#   it the default. RUST_RECORDER=false and
#   `docker compose up -d` bring the Python recorder back, no new image needed.
RUST_RECORDER=false
RUST_DAEMON=true
RUST_NAV_CORE=false
